name verbatlas-frame-info
# README.txt, FORMAT, 1. VA_frame_info.tsv:
#   "Each line contains the ID and the name of a VerbAtlas frame, separated by a tab.
#    From VerbAtlas 1.1.0, we also provide a definition, a prototypical synset (i.e.,
#    the synset that roughly represents the frame), the definition of the prototypical
#    synset, and a "small definition" of the frame."
# Every predicate below is one of those words, as the README writes it. The names after "columns" only point at a
# position in the row: "columns" takes names of one word, so the ones the README writes in several words are joined
# here and are never recorded; what is recorded is the "predicate" line.
# The file's first line is a licence line ("VerbAtlas 1.1.0 - SapienzaNLP - LICENSE: ..."), not a row.
match VA_frame_info.tsv
grammar table
comment V
columns ID name definition prototypical_synset definition_of_the_prototypical_synset small_definition

claims
subject in ID
attest name definition

claims
predicate prototypical synset
subject in ID
object in prototypical_synset

claims
predicate definition of the prototypical synset
subject in ID
object in definition_of_the_prototypical_synset

claims
predicate small definition
subject in ID
object in small_definition
